before we go a homeless man was reunited  with his family after almost a  quarter-century thanks to the kindness  of two New Jersey police officers video  shows 61 year old Jose Lopez tearfully  hugging his daughters and grandchildren  last week he lost touch with his family  after he moved to Florida suffered  several strokes and ended up homeless  determined to find them Lopez spent all  the money in his social security account  to travel to New Jersey a transit  officer found him wandering around a  train station and alerted a crisis  officer who contacted dozens of people  just days later Lopez saw his daughters  for the first time in more than 24 years  begging him in heaven  I got my two best girls a girlfriend we  always wish the best we always wish we  had him but we you know we were just  grateful for this man police helped  enroll Lopez in a mental health program  and they hope he will soon find  permanent housing near his family  everybody has a story people thanks to  that crisis workers well not only the  police sir made a lot of calls thank you  both
 

